Single-database Alembic configuration running on an async driver.

env.py resolves the database URL from app.core.config (settings.DATABASE_URL), so alembic.ini
carries no URL. With ENV=testing a TEST_DATABASE_URL environment variable takes precedence, and a
caller may instead pass an open connection through config.attributes["connection"] — that is the
path the pytest fixtures use.

Apply everything:      alembic upgrade head
Autogenerate a change: alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add shipment tables"
Inspect the SQL only:  alembic upgrade head --sql

Run these from the backend/ directory (alembic.ini sets prepend_sys_path = . so the app package is
importable). Every generated revision must be read before it is committed: autogenerate does not
detect table or column renames, server-side default changes, or check constraint edits.
